# Netlify response headers.
# Netlify already negotiates Brotli/gzip and revalidates with ETags; what it does
# not do on its own is tell the browser how long it may reuse a file without asking.
#
# There is nothing to cache but media: each page carries its own stylesheet, script
# and typefaces inline, so the page rule below governs all three.

# Photography and video change only when the clinic reshoots. A month of reuse,
# then a background refresh so nobody waits on the revalidation.
# NOTE: filenames carry no content hash. If you replace a photo but keep its name,
# give it a new name (or shorten this max-age) or repeat visitors can sit on the
# old file for up to a month.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Pages carry their own CSS, JS and fonts, so they must always be fresh.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
